From db5ecfeb7231a28cc92a19f2def439a41f06e09b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eric R. Smith" <eric.smith@collabora.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 11:12:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] pan: in register allocation, consider spilling the node being
 allocated

In some cases, we may be trying to allocate a node that is
used in a very large number of blocks. In that case, it may be
better to spill that node rather than going through the blocks
one by one spilling other registers. This actually comes up
fairly rarely in practice (because the SSA register spiller usually
prevents us from needing spills) but there are edge cases where the
LCRA and SSA allocators differ on the register pressure and LCRA
wants to spill.

Reviewed-by: Christoph Pillmayer <christoph.pillmayer@arm.com>
Signed-off-by: Eric R. Smith <eric.smith@collabora.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/42888>

(cherry picked from commit 45582c89a8c64f55784ace8daec70a6bf361e75d,
without its max_iters 2000 -> 400 hunk, which upstream reverted in
b84ccacd "panfrost: restore max retry count for bifrost LCRA spills")
Change-Id: If8195f14747ca93a7377121d1a58d175b3f2dcc1
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
index 6887ab0df51..d5b62928dbc 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
@@ -628,6 +628,15 @@ bi_choose_spill_node(bi_context *ctx, struct lcra_state *l)
    unsigned best_benefit = 0;
    signed best_node = -1;
 
+   /* consider spilling the node that we're trying to allocate,
+    * rather the ones interfering with it, if that would be
+    * better
+    */
+   if (!BITSET_TEST(no_spill, l->spill_node)) {
+      best_node = l->spill_node;
+      best_benefit = lcra_count_constraints(l, best_node);
+   }
+
    if (nodearray_is_sparse(&l->linear[l->spill_node])) {
       nodearray_sparse_foreach(&l->linear[l->spill_node], elem) {
          unsigned i = nodearray_sparse_key(elem);
